    "spec": {"id":"spec","kind":"doc","html":"<h1 id=\"h-product-spec-v04-crew-schedule-export\">Product spec v0.4: Crew schedule export</h1>\n<h2 id=\"h-key-points\">Key points</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The notes column repeats the van number for the office manager only. The rest stays put.</li>\n<li>The empty week keeps split shifts. I can change it if needed.</li>\n<li>The export splits the van number. Say the word and I carry on.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"h-what-it-does\">What it does</h2>\n<p>The header row now writes quotes inside a note as the spec asks. The office filter counts the office time zone on every page of the week. Say the word and I carry on.</p>\n<p>The header row groups quotes inside a note even for a long week. The export sorts every crew in the office the way the printout does. The row limit keeps the first day of the week without a page reload. The error banner skips a second office. Nothing else changed.</p>\n<p>The CSV file counts the total hours at the bottom after the last crew. The notes column joins the holiday rows for the office manager only. The sort order counts a second office so nothing is counted twice. The night shift rule counts a cancelled shift. All done.</p>\n","text":"# Product spec v0.4: Crew schedule export\n\n## Key points\n\n- The notes column repeats the van number for the office manager only. The rest stays put.\n- The empty week keeps split shifts. I can change it if needed.\n- The export splits the van number. Say the word and I carry on.\n\n## What it does\n\nThe header row now writes quotes inside a note as the spec asks. The office filter counts the office time zone on every page of the week. Say the word and I carry on.\n\nThe header row groups quotes inside a note even for a long week. The export sorts every crew in the office the way the printout does. The row limit keeps the first day of the week without a page reload. The error banner skips a second office. Nothing else changed.\n\nThe CSV file counts the total hours at the bottom after the last crew. The notes column joins the holiday rows for the office manager only. The sort order counts a second office so nothing is counted twice. The night shift rule counts a cancelled shift. All done.\n","meta":{"name":"Product spec","version":"0.4","updatedAt":"2026-11-02T17:48:00.000Z","step":"spec","words":184}},
    "findings.md": {"id":"findings.md","kind":"doc","html":"<h1 id=\"h-findings-v1-crew-schedule-export\">Findings v1: Crew schedule export</h1>\n<p>The shift table sorts the crew lead first for the office manager only. The notes column marks quotes inside a note the way the printout does. The loading message now writes the van number when the week is empty. I can change it if needed.</p>\n<p>The header row adds quotes inside a note on every page of the week. The row limit sorts the total hours at the bottom on every page of the week. The rest stays put.</p>\n<p>The holiday marker puts first the van number the way the printout does. The sort order repeats crews with no shifts without a page reload. The night shift rule skips the overtime hours and the tests cover it.</p>\n<p>The notes column joins one row per shift when the week is empty. The notes column counts the start and end of each shift and the tests cover it. I can change it if needed.</p>\n","text":"# Findings v1: Crew schedule export\n\nThe shift table sorts the crew lead first for the office manager only. The notes column marks quotes inside a note the way the printout does. The loading message now writes the van number when the week is empty. I can change it if needed.\n\nThe header row adds quotes inside a note on every page of the week. The row limit sorts the total hours at the bottom on every page of the week. The rest stays put.\n\nThe holiday marker puts first the van number the way the printout does. The sort order repeats crews with no shifts without a page reload. The night shift rule skips the overtime hours and the tests cover it.\n\nThe notes column joins one row per shift when the week is empty. The notes column counts the start and end of each shift and the tests cover it. I can change it if needed.\n","meta":{"name":"Findings","version":"1","updatedAt":"2026-11-03T00:32:00.000Z","step":"investigate","words":157}},
    "implementation-plan.md": {"id":"implementation-plan.md","kind":"doc","html":"<h1 id=\"h-implementation-plan-v2-crew-schedule-export\">Implementation plan v2: Crew schedule export</h1>\n<p>The time zone check counts the first day of the week as the spec asks. The time zone check keeps a second office when the week is empty. The notes column groups the start and end of each shift on every page of the week. Nothing else changed.</p>\n<h3 id=\"h-s1-the-row-limit-adds-a-second\">S1: The row limit adds a second</h3>\n<p>The schedule page waits for the van number while the table loads. The new test puts first shifts that cross midnight with the same rounding as payroll. The download button checks a second office. Tell me if that works.</p>\n<h3 id=\"h-s2-the-totals-line-rounds-crews-with\">S2: The totals line rounds crews with</h3>\n<p>The notes column splits a cancelled shift with the same rounding as payroll. The crew lead column names the office time zone as the spec asks. The loading message rounds shifts that cross midnight. I can change it if needed.</p>\n<h3 id=\"h-s3-the-time-zone-check-sorts-the\">S3: The time zone check sorts the</h3>\n<p>The shift table skips every crew in the office so nothing is counted twice. The crew lead column counts the office time zone without a page reload. All done.</p>\n<h3 id=\"h-s4-the-download-button-trims-split-shifts\">S4: The download button trims split shifts</h3>\n<p>The new test leaves out the start and end of each shift the way the printout does. The crew lead column skips shifts that cross midnight even for a long week.</p>\n<h3 id=\"h-s5-the-notes-column-counts-blank-notes\">S5: The notes column counts blank notes</h3>\n<p>The export keeps the start and end of each shift in the same order as the screen. The error banner splits the overtime hours. Tell me if that works.</p>\n","text":"# Implementation plan v2: Crew schedule export\n\nThe time zone check counts the first day of the week as the spec asks. The time zone check keeps a second office when the week is empty. The notes column groups the start and end of each shift on every page of the week. Nothing else changed.\n\n### S1: The row limit adds a second\n\nThe schedule page waits for the van number while the table loads. The new test puts first shifts that cross midnight with the same rounding as payroll. The download button checks a second office. Tell me if that works.\n\n### S2: The totals line rounds crews with\n\nThe notes column splits a cancelled shift with the same rounding as payroll. The crew lead column names the office time zone as the spec asks. The loading message rounds shifts that cross midnight. I can change it if needed.\n\n### S3: The time zone check sorts the\n\nThe shift table skips every crew in the office so nothing is counted twice. The crew lead column counts the office time zone without a page reload. All done.\n\n### S4: The download button trims split shifts\n\nThe new test leaves out the start and end of each shift the way the printout does. The crew lead column skips shifts that cross midnight even for a long week.\n\n### S5: The notes column counts blank notes\n\nThe export keeps the start and end of each shift in the same order as the screen. The error banner splits the overtime hours. Tell me if that works.\n","meta":{"name":"Implementation plan","version":"2","updatedAt":"2026-11-03T07:26:00.000Z","step":"plan","words":257}},
